<title>USA: CellNet Data sued by sharholder.</title>
<headline>CellNet Data sued by sharholder.</headline>
<dateline>SAN CARLOS, Calif. 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>CellNet Data Systems Inc said Sunday it was sued on October 31 by a shareholder who claims the company misled investors in the prospectus for an offering of 5,000,000 shares.</p>
<p>CellNet said the allegations contained in the suit, a purported class action captioned Settle vs Seidl and filed in California Superior Court in San Mateo County, are meritless and that the company will defend itself.</p>
<p>The suit names the company, some of its officers and directors and the lead underwriter for the offering, which CellNet did not indentify.</p>
<p>CellNet said the allegations centered on the company's failure to disclose the potential for a patent conflict with Itron Inc.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk  (212) 859-1610</p>
